-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]


The DWR-921 is shipped with the JBOOT [[docs:techref:bootloader|bootloader]].

Two options are theoretically possible to install the OpenWrt/LEDE firmware image:

  - Use the OEM GUI firmware upgrade feature with the OpenWrt ''-factory.bin'' image.
  - Use the JBOOT recovery service with the OpenWrt ''-factory.bin''.


==== JBOOT web recovery service ====

  - Push the reset button and turn on the power. Wait until LED starts blinking (~10sec.)
  - Access JBOOT web interface (''%%http://192.168.123.254%%'')
  - Upload ''-factory.bin'' image (or OEM firmware image if you want to go back to stock / OEM firmware) via web interface
  - If via JBOOT web interface doesn't work, it can be done on the command line with curl command:\\ ''%%curl -F FN=@XXXXX.bin http://192.168.123.254/upg%%'' where ''XXXXX.bin'' is the name of the ''-factory.bin'' file.



